@meta
id: 24-11
title: Shift lines by range
chapter: 24
type: lesson
skills: ex-shift
par: 29
minutes: 5
vscode: select the lines, Tab; select the others, Shift-Tab twice
open: order.provider.ts
vimrc: set shiftwidth=2 expandtab

@brief
Three blocks in this provider came through a paste at the wrong depth.
Line 6 and lines 12 to 13 are one level too shallow. Lines 18 to 24,
the whole body of `findOne`, are two levels too deep.

`>` and `<` are the shift commands, and they take a range like
everything else. One `>` shifts by one `shiftwidth`, two spaces here.
Doubling the character doubles the shift: `:18,24<<` pulls the lines
back two levels in one command. Blank lines inside the range are left
alone, so you can include them without thinking about it.

@keys
| `:6>` | indent line 6 by one level |
| `:12,13>` | indent lines 12 to 13 by one level |
| `:18,24<<` | outdent lines 18 to 24 by two levels |
| `:> 4` | indent four lines starting at the current one |

@hints
Three commands, three ranges. The direction of the arrow is the
direction the text moves.
--
Stack the arrows for more than one level. `<<` in a range is not the
normal-mode `<<`; it is two levels of shift.
--
`:6>` Enter, `:12,13>` Enter, `:18,24<<` Enter, `:wq`.

@solution
    :6><Enter>  :12,13><Enter>  :18,24<<<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Twenty-five keystrokes.

The range form is not much shorter than `>>` with a count, but it
composes. `:g/^  throw/>` indents every shallow `throw` in the file.
`:'a,'b>` indents between two marks. And `:18,24<<` is the only one of
these that does two levels in one go; `<<` in normal mode does one, and
you would type it twice or give it `2` as a count on the operator.

If you want the block re-indented to whatever depth is *correct* rather
than shifted by a fixed amount, that is `=`, and chapter 23 covered it.
Shift is for when you know the delta; `=` is for when you know the
answer.

@start order.provider.ts
export class OrderProvider {
  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
    throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
    where: { id },
    values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async findOne(id: string) {
        const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

        if (!order) {
          throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
        }

        return order;
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
export class OrderProvider {
  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }
}
